    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0226" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg206"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">357.AD/6–2750: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in The Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Chapin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-27T16:00:00+01:00">June 27, 1950—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 27—2:05 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>779. When I delivered substance Department’s 635 June 27<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d124-f1"/> to Stikker he stated as a first reaction, “I am mighty
                    glad that the US <pb facs="0227" n="207" xml:id="pg207"/> has taken this
                    action.” In taking my leave he added, “US may count on all possible support from
                    Netherlands Government in UN.”</p>
                <p>Repeated info Paris 179, London 194, Moscow 15, Brussels 41.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d124-f1" n="1" xml:id="d124-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 3124, June 27, 1 a. m., to London, <ref target="#pg186">p. 186</ref>,
                    was repeated to The Hague as telegram 635.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
